1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:01,590
Curd bacteria.

2
00:00:01,590 --> 00:00:03,679
A green cell in pond water.

3
00:00:03,679 --> 00:00:04,713
Bread mould.

4
00:00:04,713 --> 00:00:05,864
A mango tree.

5
00:00:05,864 --> 00:00:06,764
A cat.

6
00:00:06,978 --> 00:00:08,271
Five living things.

7
00:00:08,271 --> 00:00:10,390
Two kingdoms could not hold them.

8
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:14,678
Diya had sorted them into five
boxes with her own questions.

9
00:00:14,678 --> 00:00:19,184
Then she found that a scientist had
done the same, more than fifty years

10
00:00:19,184 --> 00:00:20,084
ago.

11
00:00:20,034 --> 00:00:23,527
His five boxes are still
the ones in your NCERT book.

12
00:00:23,977 --> 00:00:28,213
By the end, you will know all five
kingdoms, and build their comparison

13
00:00:28,213 --> 00:00:29,249
table yourself.

14
00:00:29,899 --> 00:00:35,098
In nineteen sixty nine, RH Whittaker
proposed a five kingdom classification.

15
00:00:35,448 --> 00:00:36,348
Monera.

16
00:00:36,191 --> 00:00:37,091
Protista.

17
00:00:37,047 --> 00:00:37,947
Fungi.

18
00:00:37,734 --> 00:00:38,634
Plantae.

19
00:00:38,533 --> 00:00:39,682
And Animalia.

20
00:00:40,132 --> 00:00:42,185
He used five main criteria.

21
00:00:42,185 --> 00:00:47,090
Cell structure, body organisation,
mode of nutrition, reproduction, and

22
00:00:47,090 --> 00:00:48,949
phylogenetic relationships.

23
00:00:49,599 --> 00:00:52,313
Watch the two old boxes break into five.

24
00:00:52,663 --> 00:00:54,324
All bacteria leave Plantae.

25
00:00:54,324 --> 00:00:58,494
They have no nuclear membrane, so
they get their own kingdom, Monera.

26
00:00:58,944 --> 00:01:00,556
Fungi leave Plantae too.

27
00:01:00,556 --> 00:01:04,287
They cannot make food, and
their walls are made of chitin.

28
00:01:04,287 --> 00:01:05,308
Kingdom Fungi.

29
00:01:05,758 --> 00:01:09,772
Chlamydomonas and Chlorella were
called algae, inside Plantae.

30
00:01:09,772 --> 00:01:11,345
Both have cell walls.

31
00:01:11,795 --> 00:01:14,743
Amoeba and Paramoecium
were called animals.

32
00:01:14,743 --> 00:01:16,387
Both lack cell walls.

33
00:01:16,837 --> 00:01:21,395
Whittaker put all four together in
Protista, because each one is a single

34
00:01:21,395 --> 00:01:22,609
celled eukaryote.

35
00:01:23,109 --> 00:01:27,703
What stays behind in Plantae and
Animalia are the many celled plants and

36
00:01:27,703 --> 00:01:28,603
animals.

37
00:01:29,090 --> 00:01:33,139
Now let's build Whittaker's
comparison table, one row at a time.

38
00:01:33,490 --> 00:01:35,117
Row one, cell type.

39
00:01:35,117 --> 00:01:36,786
Monera are prokaryotic.

40
00:01:36,786 --> 00:01:39,490
The other four kingdoms are eukaryotic.

41
00:01:40,240 --> 00:01:41,774
Row two, cell wall.

42
00:01:41,774 --> 00:01:44,642
Monera have a wall, but not of cellulose.

43
00:01:44,642 --> 00:01:46,375
Some protists have walls.

44
00:01:46,375 --> 00:01:47,699
Fungi have chitin.

45
00:01:47,699 --> 00:01:49,223
Plants have cellulose.

46
00:01:49,223 --> 00:01:51,065
Animals have no cell wall.

47
00:01:51,815 --> 00:01:53,715
Row three, nuclear membrane.

48
00:01:53,715 --> 00:01:57,553
It is absent only in Monera,
and present in the other four.

49
00:01:58,303 --> 00:02:00,366
Row four, body organisation.

50
00:02:00,366 --> 00:02:02,812
Monera and Protista are just cells.

51
00:02:02,812 --> 00:02:05,735
Fungi are many celled, with loose tissue.

52
00:02:05,735 --> 00:02:07,912
Plants have tissues and organs.

53
00:02:07,912 --> 00:02:10,566
Animals go further, to organ systems.

54
00:02:11,316 --> 00:02:13,542
Row five, mode of nutrition.

55
00:02:13,542 --> 00:02:16,008
Monera can make food or take it.

56
00:02:16,008 --> 00:02:17,344
So can Protista.

57
00:02:17,344 --> 00:02:19,115
Fungi are heterotrophic.

58
00:02:19,115 --> 00:02:20,831
Plants are autotrophic.

59
00:02:20,831 --> 00:02:22,710
Animals are heterotrophic.

60
00:02:23,460 --> 00:02:26,929
Two kingdoms look alike,
because both are single cells.

61
00:02:26,929 --> 00:02:28,197
Let's compare them.

62
00:02:28,547 --> 00:02:31,082
Monera, like the bacterium in curd.

63
00:02:31,082 --> 00:02:34,895
One small cell, and no nuclear
membrane around its DNA.

64
00:02:35,345 --> 00:02:37,043
Protista, like Amoeba.

65
00:02:37,043 --> 00:02:42,033
Also one cell, but a eukaryotic cell,
with a true nucleus inside a nuclear

66
00:02:42,033 --> 00:02:42,933
membrane.

67
00:02:43,424 --> 00:02:44,374
Your turn.

68
00:02:44,374 --> 00:02:47,573
Paramoecium is one cell
with a true nucleus.

69
00:02:47,573 --> 00:02:49,080
Monera or Protista?

70
00:02:49,080 --> 00:02:50,478
Pause and decide.

71
00:02:53,678 --> 00:02:54,578
Protista!

72
00:02:54,429 --> 00:02:57,739
It has a nuclear membrane,
so it is a eukaryote.

73
00:02:57,739 --> 00:02:59,004
Monera have none.

74
00:02:59,654 --> 00:03:00,813
Remember this.

75
00:03:00,813 --> 00:03:01,973
Five kingdoms.

76
00:03:01,973 --> 00:03:05,331
Monera, Protista, Fungi,
Plantae, Animalia.

77
00:03:05,931 --> 00:03:07,508
Now, a worked example.

78
00:03:07,508 --> 00:03:10,437
Six living things, with
the table as our key.

79
00:03:10,787 --> 00:03:13,296
Anabaena has no nuclear membrane.

80
00:03:13,296 --> 00:03:14,196
Monera.

81
00:03:14,499 --> 00:03:17,213
Paramoecium is one eukaryotic cell.

82
00:03:17,213 --> 00:03:18,113
Protista.

83
00:03:18,559 --> 00:03:23,290
Chlamydomonas is one eukaryotic
cell too, even though it is green.

84
00:03:23,290 --> 00:03:24,190
Protista.

85
00:03:24,574 --> 00:03:29,839
Yeast is one cell, but it is a true
fungus, a sac fungus like Penicillium.

86
00:03:29,839 --> 00:03:30,739
Fungi.

87
00:03:30,975 --> 00:03:34,562
A fern has cellulose walls
and makes its own food.

88
00:03:34,562 --> 00:03:35,462
Plantae.

89
00:03:35,322 --> 00:03:38,021
An earthworm has no wall, and eats.

90
00:03:38,021 --> 00:03:38,921
Animalia.

91
00:03:39,485 --> 00:03:40,950
Now, the exam trap.

92
00:03:41,300 --> 00:03:45,301
Many students think every single
celled living thing is a protist.

93
00:03:45,701 --> 00:03:50,949
But bacteria are single cells in Monera,
and yeast is a single celled fungus.

94
00:03:50,949 --> 00:03:53,604
Protista means single celled eukaryotes.

95
00:03:54,254 --> 00:03:55,667
Where is this asked?

96
00:03:55,667 --> 00:04:00,142
As match the following on kingdom
features, or statements from the comparison

97
00:04:00,142 --> 00:04:01,042
table.

98
00:04:01,320 --> 00:04:02,510
Exam level now.

99
00:04:02,510 --> 00:04:04,939
Match each kingdom with its feature.

100
00:04:04,939 --> 00:04:06,179
Pause and solve.

101
00:04:11,579 --> 00:04:12,720
The answer is C.

102
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:14,958
a three, b one, c four, d two.

103
00:04:15,458 --> 00:04:19,614
Monera have a wall that is not
cellulose, and no nuclear membrane.

104
00:04:20,114 --> 00:04:21,447
Fungi have chitin.

105
00:04:21,447 --> 00:04:22,980
Plants have cellulose.

106
00:04:22,980 --> 00:04:24,834
Animals have no cell wall.

107
00:04:25,434 --> 00:04:26,893
Here is your recap.

108
00:04:26,893 --> 00:04:28,393
Screenshot this card.

109
00:04:31,593 --> 00:04:34,429
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

110
00:04:34,829 --> 00:04:35,729
One.

111
00:04:35,338 --> 00:04:38,908
Who proposed the five kingdom
classification, and when?

112
00:04:39,808 --> 00:04:40,708
Two.

113
00:04:40,331 --> 00:04:42,906
Which kingdom has no nuclear membrane?

114
00:04:43,806 --> 00:04:44,706
Three.

115
00:04:44,399 --> 00:04:48,042
Why were Chlamydomonas and
Amoeba put in the same kingdom?

116
00:04:49,142 --> 00:04:51,823
Next time: milk turns into curd overnight.

117
00:04:51,823 --> 00:04:53,122
Who does the work?

118
00:04:53,122 --> 00:04:55,093
We find out in kingdom Monera.
